either matches.\n- **LiAl(SiO3)2:** a silicate would give many peaks between 20\u00b0 and 30\u00b0, a range that is nearly empty here.\n\n{\"present\": [\"mp-1646508\"], \"confidence\": 0.7, \"note\": \"A strong 19.15\u00b0 B-site ordering peak (Fe/W) plus split perovskite reflections near 31-32\u00b0, 45\u00b0 and 56.5\u00b0 fit triclinic CaLaFeWO6, though the 32.25\u00b0 maximum sits slightly higher than estimated; no other candidate matches.\"}",
